# Scripts MUST be LF in the repository. Git's autocrlf on Windows would commit
# CRLF, and a clone on Linux or macOS then fails with
#   bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M
# before a single line of the script runs. The memory store this tooling seals
# has the opposite requirement (`* -text`, bytes preserved exactly, because the
# seal hashes them); both are the same hazard with opposite fixes.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
hook/*  text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
